      "description": "Path traversal (CWE-22) at download_archive: the user-controlled 'filename' is joined directly onto STORAGE_ROOT and passed to open() without confinement. An attacker can submit a value like '../../etc/passwd' to read arbitrary files. Static evidence from sast-scan confirms AST_PATH_TRAVERSAL at line 8; risk-classify flags SECURITY_SENSITIVE_PATH (L2).",
      "category": "injection",
      "severity": "high",
      "risk_level": "L2"
